@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Me";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<div class="row mt-4">
    <div class="col-md-12">
        <h2>Hi, I'm Grant Kollar</h2>
        <p class="lead">
            I'm a student studying software development with a passion for the outdoors, especially skiing.
        </p>
        <p>
            I grew up in the Midwest but discovered skiing and immediately fell in love with the mountains.
            Every winter I try to get out to the slopes as much as possible, whether that's a quick day trip
            or a full week-long trip out west.
        </p>
        <p>
            This website is my final project for my ASP.NET MVC web development course. I built it to document
            and share my love of skiing, covering everything from my favorite resorts to the gear I rely on
            every season.
        </p>

        <h3 class="mt-4">Skills &amp; Interests</h3>
        <ul>
            <li>Software Development (C#, ASP.NET Core, SQL)</li>
            <li>Alpine / Downhill Skiing</li>
            <li>Hiking &amp; Outdoor Adventure</li>
            <li>Following ski resort conditions and snowfall reports</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="mt-4">Skiing Experience</h3>
        <p>
            I would describe myself as an intermediate-to-advanced skier. I'm comfortable on black diamond runs
            and enjoy pushing myself on steeper terrain. My favorite type of skiing is groomed carving in the
            morning before the crowds hit the mountain.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
